note open/route.om: Open Humanity's shelf of open builds, inside forged. Prefix oh* (functions),
note go* (globals), to* (texts). Composed after the salvage and social slices, whose form reader,
note write precheck and session it uses (slformvalid, slgetform, slffeq, sowpre, soratev, soerr).
note A person signed in with a Radicle key names the Radicle id (RID) of a project that is not
note finished, or not right yet. forged does not fetch anything: it has no network and cannot run
note rad. It appends one line to <data>open/queue and the intake service (open/intake.om, its own
note program outside the sandbox) seeds and fetches the project within limits and rewrites
note <data>open/list.tsv, which this unit shows.
note   GET  <base>open/   the shelf: every project the intake accepted, marked unfinished and not
note                      verified, with its rad clone line; JSON when the request asks for it
note   POST <base>open/   action=bring (rid, note, consent=yes) or action=withdraw (rid)
note Queue lines:  B <tab> rid <tab> did <tab> note     and     W <tab> rid <tab> did
note list.tsv rows: rid, state, did, date, kilobytes, name, description, note. States "open" and
note "held" are listed for everyone; any other state is shown only to the key that brought the
note project.
note Every field is escaped on output. The queue is capped at 1 MiB (503 beyond it).
text topath "/open/"
text topat2 "/open"
text todir "open/"
text toq "queue"
text tolist "list.tsv"
text toti "Open builds"
text torid "rid"
text tonote "note"
text tocons "consent"
text toyes "yes"
text toact "action"
text tobring "bring"
text towith "withdraw"
text tostop "open"
text toheld "held"
text tob58 "123456789ABCDEFGHJKLMNPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijkmnopqrstuvwxyz"
text torad "rad:"
text tologin "login"
text tomsg1 "The form was refused. Give the Radicle id of your project (rad:z...), tick the permission box, and keep the note under 200 bytes."
text tomsgq "The intake queue is full. Nothing was saved. Try again later."
text toh1 "<div class=\"sl\"><h1>Open builds</h1><p>Bring the project that is not finished, or not right yet. It stays open here so other builders and their agents can pick it up over Radicle. Nothing on this shelf is verified until a revision carries a receipt.</p>"
text toh2 "<article class=\"sl-card\"><h2>Bring a project</h2><p>Publish it to Radicle first (<code>rad init</code>, then <code>rad sync --announce</code>), then give its id. This node fetches it and keeps a copy available. Limits: 50 MiB a project, 8 open projects a key. Intake is open to invited keys for now; a key that is not on the list sees the refusal here. You can withdraw it at any time.</p>"
text toh3 "<p><a href=\""
text toh4 "\">Sign in with your Radicle key</a> to bring a project.</p></article>"
text tof1 "<form method=\"post\" action=\""
text tof2 "\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"csrf\" value=\""
text tof3 "\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"action\" value=\"bring\"><p><label>Radicle id <input name=\"rid\" maxlength=\"48\" required placeholder=\"rad:z...\"></label></p><p><label>What is unfinished, in one line <input name=\"note\" maxlength=\"200\"></label></p><p><label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"consent\" value=\"yes\" required> I have the right to share this project and it carries an open license.</label></p><p><button type=\"submit\">Bring it</button></p></form></article>"
text tol1 "<h2>On the shelf</h2>"
text tol0 "<p>The shelf is waiting for its first project. Unfinished is welcome.</p>"
text toc1 "<article class=\"sl-card\"><h3>"
text toc2 "</h3><p>"
text toc3 "</p><p><strong>Unfinished:</strong> "
text toc4 "</p><pre>rad clone rad:"
text toc5 "</pre><p>Not verified. Brought by "
text toc6 " on "
text toc7 ", "
text toc8 " KiB.</p>"
text toc9 "</article>"
text tow1 "\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"action\" value=\"withdraw\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"rid\" value=\""
text tow2 "\"><button type=\"submit\">Withdraw</button></form>"
text tor1 "<article class=\"sl-card\"><h3>rad:"
text tor2 "</h3><p>Only you see this. Intake result: "
text tor3 "</p></article>"
text toend "</div>"
text toj1 "{\"schema\":\"interplane/open-builds/1\",\"note\":\"unfinished projects brought over Radicle; nothing here is verified\",\"projects\":["
text toj2 "{\"rid\":\"rad:"
text toj3 "\",\"brought_by\":\""
text toj4 "\",\"date\":\""
text toj5 "\",\"kib\":"
text toj6 ",\"name\":\""
text toj7 "\",\"description\":\""
text toj8 "\",\"unfinished\":\""
text toj9 "\",\"verified\":false}"
text toj10 "]}\n"
text toctj "application/json; charset=utf-8"
text tohex "0123456789abcdef"
text tou00 "\\u00"
global gorid uchar 48
global goridl ulong 1
global godid uchar 96
global godidl ulong 1
global gonote uchar 208
global gonotel ulong 1
global gol uchar 262144
global goll ulong 1
note ohb58: c is a base58 character
fn ohb58 c uchar to bool
for i ulong len tob58 bound 64
if eq get tob58 i c
ret true
end
end
ret false
end
note ohrid: the form value gcfv[0, n) as a RID into gorid: an optional "rad:", then z and base58,
note 20 to 44 characters in all
fn ohrid n ulong to bool
a = ulong 0
if ge n 4
same = true
for i ulong 4
if ne get gcfv i get torad i
same = false
end
end
if same
a = ulong 4
end
end
m = sub n a
if or lt m 20 gt m 44
ret false
end
if ne get gcfv a 122
ret false
end
for i ulong m bound 44
c = get gcfv add a i
if not ohb58 c
ret false
end
put gorid i c
end
put goridl 0 m
ret true
end
note ohdid: the signed-in key's DID into godid. False when signed out or the string is not plain.
fn ohdid to bool
who = get gscur 0
if eq who 0
ret false
end
n = get gssl who
if or eq n 0 gt n 96
ret false
end
o = get gsso who
for i ulong n bound 96
c = get gsstr add o i
if or le c 32 ge c 127
ret false
end
put godid i c
end
put godidl 0 n
ret true
end
note ohnote: the form value gcfv[0, n) into gonote: at most 200 bytes, control bytes become spaces
fn ohnote n ulong to bool
if gt n 200
ret false
end
for i ulong n bound 200
c = get gcfv i
if or lt c 32 eq c 127
c = uchar 32
end
put gonote i c
end
put gonotel 0 n
ret true
end
note ohfile: ffile = <data>open/<name>
fn ohfile name view uchar * to void
put ffilel 0 0
for i ulong len tfdata bound 128
ffilc get tfdata i
end
for i ulong len todir bound 16
ffilc get todir i
end
for i ulong len name bound 16
ffilc get name i
end
end
note ohappend: one queue line of the given kind (66 B or 87 W). 0 done, else the status to answer.
fn ohappend kind uchar to long
b = new uchar 400 0
st = new uchar 128 0
ohfile tostop
put ffilel 0 sub get ffilel 0 len tostop
r = makedir ffile 0 get ffilel 0 448
ohfile toq
fd = fopen ffile 0 get ffilel 0 558145 384
if lt fd 0
ret 503
end
r = fstat int fd st 0 128
sz = or or ulong get st 48 shl ulong get st 49 8 or shl ulong get st 50 16 shl ulong get st 51 24
if or ne r 0 gt sz 1048576
x = fclose int fd
ret 503
end
n = ulong 0
put b 0 kind
put b 1 9
n = ulong 2
for i ulong get goridl 0 bound 44
put b add n i get gorid i
end
n = add n get goridl 0
put b n 9
n = add n 1
for i ulong get godidl 0 bound 96
put b add n i get godid i
end
n = add n get godidl 0
if eq kind 66
put b n 9
n = add n 1
for i ulong get gonotel 0 bound 200
put b add n i get gonote i
end
n = add n get gonotel 0
end
put b n 10
n = add n 1
w = write int fd b 0 n
x = fclose int fd
if ne w long n
ret 503
end
ret 0
end
note ohgo: 303 to <base>open/
fn ohgo to long
flocb
floct todir
put fkind 0 2
ret 303
end
fn ohpost to long
r = sowpre
if ne r 0
ret r
end
soratev get gscur 0 get gsnow 0
if not slformvalid
ret soerr 400 tomsg1
end
if ne slgetform tsfcsrf 32
ret soerr 400 tomsg1
end
if not ohdid
ret 403
end
n = slgetform torid
if le n 0
ret soerr 400 tomsg1
end
if not ohrid ulong n
ret soerr 400 tomsg1
end
if slffeq toact towith
r = ohappend 87
if ne r 0
ret soerr 503 tomsgq
end
ret ohgo
end
if not slffeq toact tobring
ret soerr 400 tomsg1
end
if not slffeq tocons toyes
ret soerr 400 tomsg1
end
n = slgetform tonote
if lt n 0
ret soerr 400 tomsg1
end
if not ohnote ulong n
ret soerr 400 tomsg1
end
r = ohappend 66
if ne r 0
ret soerr 503 tomsgq
end
ret ohgo
end
note ---- the list
fn ohload to void
put goll 0 0
ohfile tolist
fd = fopen ffile 0 get ffilel 0 557056 0
if lt fd 0
ret
end
n = ulong 0
k = long 1
while gt k 0 bound 262144
k = read int fd gol n sub 262143 n
if gt k 0
n = add n ulong k
end
end
x = fclose int fd
put goll 0 n
end
fn oheol a ulong to ulong
lim = get goll 0
i = a
while lt i lim bound 262144
if eq get gol i 10
ret i
end
i = add i 1
end
ret lim
end
note ohfld: start of field k of the row s..e (e when the row has fewer fields)
fn ohfld s ulong e ulong k ulong to ulong
p = s
j = ulong 0
while lt j k bound 16
while lt p e bound 262144
if eq get gol p 9
break
end
p = add p 1
end
if lt p e
p = add p 1
end
j = add j 1
end
ret p
end
fn ohfe a ulong e ulong to ulong
p = a
while lt p e bound 262144
if eq get gol p 9
ret p
end
p = add p 1
end
ret e
end
note ohesc / ohjs: field k of the row s..e, HTML-escaped or as JSON string bytes, at most cap bytes
fn ohesc s ulong e ulong k ulong cap ulong to void
a = ohfld s e k
b = ohfe a e
if gt sub b a cap
b = add a cap
end
i = a
while lt i b bound 262144
c = get gol i
if ge c 32
fescc c
end
i = add i 1
end
end
fn ohjs s ulong e ulong k ulong cap ulong to void
a = ohfld s e k
b = ohfe a e
if gt sub b a cap
b = add a cap
end
i = a
while lt i b bound 262144
c = get gol i
if or eq c 34 eq c 92
fputc 92
fputc c
else
if lt c 32
fput tou00
fputc get tohex ulong shr c 4
fputc get tohex ulong and c 15
else
fputc c
end
end
i = add i 1
end
end
note ohis: field k of the row equals t
fn ohis s ulong e ulong k ulong t view uchar * to bool
a = ohfld s e k
b = ohfe a e
if ne sub b a len t
ret false
end
for i ulong len t bound 64
if ne get gol add a i get t i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note ohpub: the row is on the shelf: state open (fetched by the intake) or held (the node already
note had the project)
fn ohpub s ulong e ulong to bool
if ohis s e 1 tostop
ret true
end
ret ohis s e 1 toheld
end
note ohmine: the row's did (field 2) is the signed-in key (godid)
fn ohmine s ulong e ulong to bool
n = get godidl 0
if eq n 0
ret false
end
a = ohfld s e 2
b = ohfe a e
if ne sub b a n
ret false
end
for i ulong n bound 96
if ne get gol add a i get godid i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note ohrow: a row needs its 8 fields and a well-formed rid
fn ohrow s ulong e ulong to bool
a = ohfld s e 7
if gt a e
ret false
end
if eq a e
if lt e 1
ret false
end
if ne get gol sub e 1 9
ret false
end
end
b = ohfe s e
n = sub b s
if or lt n 20 gt n 44
ret false
end
for i ulong n bound 44
if not ohb58 get gol add s i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
fn ohcard s ulong e ulong to void
fput toc1
ohesc s e 5 120
fput toc2
ohesc s e 6 400
fput toc3
ohesc s e 7 200
fput toc4
ohesc s e 0 44
fput toc5
ohesc s e 2 96
fput toc6
ohesc s e 3 10
fput toc7
ohesc s e 4 10
fput toc8
if ohmine s e
fput tof1
fputb
fput todir
fput tof2
socsrfout
fput tow1
ohesc s e 0 44
fput tow2
end
fput toc9
end
fn ohrefused s ulong e ulong to void
fput tor1
ohesc s e 0 44
fput tor2
ohesc s e 1 80
fput tor3
end
fn ohlist to void
lim = get goll 0
n = ulong 0
fput tol1
s = ulong 0
while lt s lim bound 4096
e = oheol s
if ohrow s e
if ohpub s e
ohcard s e
n = add n 1
else
if ohmine s e
ohrefused s e
end
end
end
s = add e 1
end
if eq n 0
fput tol0
end
end
note ohnum: field 4 (kilobytes) as a number
fn ohnum s ulong e ulong to ulong
a = ohfld s e 4
b = ohfe a e
v = ulong 0
i = a
while lt i b bound 12
c = get gol i
if and ge c 48 le c 57
v = add mul v 10 ulong sub c 48
end
i = add i 1
end
ret v
end
fn ohjson to long
lim = get goll 0
n = ulong 0
put fkind 0 1
fsetct toctj
fput toj1
s = ulong 0
while lt s lim bound 4096
e = oheol s
if ohrow s e
if ohpub s e
if gt n 0
fputc 44
end
fput toj2
ohjs s e 0 44
fput toj3
ohjs s e 2 96
fput toj4
ohjs s e 3 10
fput toj5
fnum ohnum s e
fput toj6
ohjs s e 5 120
fput toj7
ohjs s e 6 400
fput toj8
ohjs s e 7 200
fput toj9
n = add n 1
end
end
s = add e 1
end
fput toj10
ret 200
end
fn ohpage to long
ohload
put godidl 0 0
signed = ohdid
if fjwant
ret ohjson
end
put fkind 0 0
fsetti toti
fput toh1
fput toh2
if signed
fput tof1
fputb
fput todir
fput tof2
socsrfout
fput tof3
else
fput toh3
fputb
fput tologin
fput toh4
end
ohlist
fput toend
ret 200
end
note ohroute: 0 = not an open-builds path
fn ohroute to long
if fpeq topat2
flocb
floct todir
put fkind 0 2
ret 301
end
if not fpeq topath
ret 0
end
if eq get fmeth 0 3
ret ohpost
end
if not fget
ret 405
end
ret ohpage
end
